**Finding.** Lazy activation does open a permission TOCTOU gap if the decision is cached at index or selection. Declared permissions can change on disk between those points. The authoritative check has to re-read the live declaration and call `permissions.evaluate` immediately before materializing (activation time). Selection-time is not enough: an edit between select and activate still slips.

**Evidence (scratch copy, live evaluator).** Sequence: index `fs:read:packages/**` → edit in a tempfile catalog to add `secrets:read:**` → activate.

| Check epoch | After the edit |
|---|---|
| INDEX | slips — widened grant is materialized |
| ACTIVATION | caught — refuse, effective grant empty |
| SELECTION | catches a pre-select edit, slips a post-select edit |

**Live surface.** 12 activation entry points listed with `file:line`. Plugin `_activate` (`lifecycle.py:446`) has zero `evaluate` calls. Marketplace gate 5 (`install.py:343`) evaluates at **install** time only. The proposed A4 gateway has 7 entry points; all go through `Gateway.activate`.

